              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "aburrido — \"bored; boring\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "La película es aburrida. The film is boring."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "With estar it means bored (estoy aburrido); with ser it means boring (es aburrido)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "aburrido is the participle of aburrir, \"to bore\", from Latin abhorrere, \"to shrink back from, to shudder at\" (Lewis & Short) — inherited. With the ending -ecer, the same Latin verb also gave aborrecer, \"to loathe\"."
            }
          ]
        },
